        <mxCell id="card-steps" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#059669&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Request path · a metric from EKS&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; Alloy (cluster=aws) remote_writes to onprem-apps.cnp-vpn :18080, the cloud end of the tunnel.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; socat in the cloud WireGuard pod relays it to the on-prem tunnel IP 100.96.0.2 :18080.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;3&lt;/span&gt; The on-prem WireGuard pod relays it to vminsert :8480 (/insert/0/prometheus).&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;4&lt;/span&gt; vminsert writes to vmstorage :8400: 20 GiB on ceph-block, 14 days.&lt;br&gt;• Logs and audit events take the same road as the lettered flows below.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="620" y="1420" width="620" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-bg" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ea580c&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Background&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;A&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;B&lt;/span&gt; The on-prem pods open the tunnels (UDP 31820). &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;C&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;D&lt;/span&gt; Each cloud Alloy scrapes its pods, node-exporter and kube-state-metrics, and tails pod logs.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;E&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;F&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;G&lt;/span&gt; Logs take the same road on :18082 to the Loki gateway (basic auth alloy, password from Vault via observability-role).&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;H&lt;/span&gt; to &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;M&lt;/span&gt; GKE does the same with label cluster=gcp, tunnel 100.96.0.4/30.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;N&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;O&lt;/span&gt; On-prem Alloy (cluster=onprem) scrapes the hub and tails K3s audit.log, Vault audit, Keycloak events and Hubble policy drops.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;P&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;Q&lt;/span&gt; It writes straight to vminsert and the Loki gateway. &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;R&lt;/span&gt; Alloy sets the tenant (project label, else default); the gateway checks the client and passes it to Loki. &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;S&lt;/span&gt; Loki keeps chunks in loki-data on Ceph RGW.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;T&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;U&lt;/span&gt; Every hour audit-archive exports the audit streams and puts them in cnp-audit-archive (Object Lock, 30 days).&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;V&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;W&lt;/span&gt; :18083 carries reads of vmselect for Argo Rollouts: see observability-read.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1280" y="1420" width="820" height="400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-allow" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#e11d48&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Who may write&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Clouds&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;: NetworkPolicy onprem-apps (ns cnp-vpn) admits ns observability on 18080, 18082 and ns argo-rollouts on 18083.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;vminsert&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;: vminsert-writers admits Alloy, vmalert and the wireguard / wireguard-gcp pods.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;vmstorage&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;: vmstorage-cluster-only admits vminsert and vmselect.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Loki&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;: loki-gateway-only admits the gateway. Each client has its own basic-auth user (alloy, grafana, archive, cmp, grafana-projects).&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Retention&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;: Loki 14 days by default, 7 or 30 days by label; audit streams 30 days.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2140" y="1420" width="720" height="280" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-gaps" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ea580c&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Gaps&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#c2410c&quot;&gt;GO1&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; vminsert has no auth: the cloud cluster label is set by the client. Any pod of ns observability on a cloud may write.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#c2410c&quot;&gt;GO2&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; The Loki gateway :80 has no NetworkPolicy: basic auth alone protects it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#c2410c&quot;&gt;GO4&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; EKS and GKE API server audit, cloud Vault and Keycloak events are not collected.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="620" y="1640" width="620" height="180" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
